having encountered a friendly human, ehhhh no it was the delphic
oracle, yeah that's it, the delphic oracle while walking around,
ehhh no while rebuilding the dungeon, yeah, rebuilding the dungeon
i asked him about engravings. _he_ said that future dungeons could
indeed have an engraving lore. there would essentially be two classes
of engravings: the lesser and the greater engravings.

the lesser engravings would simply be the _extrinsic_ names of scrolls
(i.e. the intrinsic name of a scroll of fire is fire and its extrinsic
name in a particular game could be ZELGO MER). the act of engraving in
the rock (not merely writing in the dust) the extrinsic name of a scroll
might cause something to happen enabling you to deduce the identity of
certain scrolls. a problem with lesser engravings is that after
writing them you're paralyzed for 3 to 18 of moves. noticing a lesser
engraving is uneventful. currently (nh3.0 pl6) there are 21 scrolls.
in addition to paralysis the following things could happen:
INTRINSIC NAME  EFFECT
identify        enlightenment (20% chance)
teleportation   create leprechaun (50%)
amnesia         amnesia (50%)
punishment      punishment (50%)
enchant weapon  destroy wielded weapon (20% chance)
blank paper     nothing (100%)
taming          loud music [i.e. aggravate monster] (50%)
enchant armor   destroy worn armor (20% chance)
create monster  create monster (20% chance)
genocide        suicide (50%)
food detection  detect food (50%)
magic mapping   forget floor plan (50%)
fire            blindness for duration of paralysis (50%)
destroy armor   destroy worn armor (50%)
remove curse    destroy armor, weapon, rings, amulet (50%)
light           blindness for duration of paralysis (50%)
gold detection  detect gold (50%)
scare monster   same rules as Elbereth (100%)
charging        electric surge damage (20%)
confuse monster loud noise [i.e. aggravate monster] (50%)
mail            death threat via mail (20%) ... okay, nothing (100%)
as you can see writing lesser engravings is problematic:
1) you must engrave in the rock, any bladed weapon could do this but
    will become dull in the process (except athame).
2) the effects are not typically friendly, you could die!
3) the effects don't always happen, requiring persistence.
4) the effects require some deduction to identify scrolls.
5) you're paralyzed for 3-18 moves.

the greater engravings, like the lesser engravings must be engraved in
the rock! the greater engravings require the use of the create trap
spell which was suggested previously. the spell properly used in
conjunction with magic would enable the creation of many diverse trap
types otherwise it might simply create landmines or nothing. the spell
when cast in the direction of a greater engraving would create
constructs (currently either a sink or altar).  however, the magic is
not guaranteed to work (20% nominal chance of success on non-maze
levels) and when it fails the engraving is partly damaged. the greater
engravings are determined by the gods at the start of a game and
consist of a random string of 12 characters where at least one is a
number. you may learn of a greater engraving by devotion to your god or
by noticing the elven runes on special elven doors. first you must
notice the elven door which requires that you search in its vicinity
and then you must notice the runes upon that door which require that
you apply a mirror in the direction of the door. you'll see the mirror
image about 1% or 2% of the time otherwise you'll see nothing, oracles
would know this. when you see something (in your mirror) it could be a
greater engraving or the tune (5 notes) to open the drawbridge. also,
there's a extremely slight chance that you could _blindly_ bump into an
elven door and feel the runes correctly.

in review, although it possible to discover engravings and the related
lore, it would normally require a major consultation with the oracle to
discover the lore. given that you understand the lore you must then
discover the current runes and their effects which is problematic.

